{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_vrjyrymeinzmku5xmhesyzaaeyvf6wgokqvsk5op5bbpjks7ojka","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Build succeeds with no errors and only warnings on the test files (which I'm not supposed to modify).\n\nSummary of the implementation:\n\nI translated the C base122 encoder/decoder library to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n1. **`Base122Error`** — Simple error struct with a message; added `Display` and `Error` trait implementations.\n\n2. **`BitReader`** — Reads up to 8 bits at a time from a byte slice. The C version stored `len` and `curBit`; the Rust struct uses `byte_pos`/`bit_pos` (a combined `cur_bit = byte_pos*8 + bit_pos` is computed internally). Returns `(bits_read, value)`.\n\n3. **`BitWriter`** — Writes up to 8 bits to an optional `&mut [u8]`. When `output` is `None`, only counts bits (`count_only` mode) for size pre-computation. Returns the running byte count or an error if the buffer is full.\n\n4. **`encode`/`encode_internal`** — Two-pass encoding: first pass with `output=None` to compute exact size, second pass writes the result. Mirrors the C `OUTPUT_BYTE` macro via a closure. Handles the illegal-character escape sequence (two-byte form prefixed with `0xC2 | (illegal_index << 2) | first_bit`).\n\n5. **`decode`/`decode_internal`** — Two-pass decoding. Validates the two-byte sequence prefix (`110xxx1y` / `10xxxxxx`), the special \"shortened\" form (`illegal_index == 0x7`), and uses `write_last_7` for the final byte to enforce byte alignment.\n\n6. **`write_last_7`** — Writes the trailing partial byte to the bit stream while validating that no extra bits are set beyond the byte boundary.\n\nAll 6 tests pass (`test_bit_reader`, `test_bit_writer`, `test_decode_error_cases`, `test_decode_success_cases`, `test_encode_all_ones`, `test_roundtrip`); `test_encode_file` is `#[ignore]` because it requires example data files. No `unsafe`, no FFI, no `unimplemented!()` placeholders remain."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"cache_read_input_tokens":45402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":341,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e364dba-9b11-44c4-994c-32ab23ce2165","uuid":"9d889f96-0048-4cff-9c53-6ad359f70aeb"}
